tune by \u00b11 next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s commit to a clearer stance with a bolder yet still incremental move. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "\nLow positive options have strong support; nudging one step higher keeps balance while testing comfort with a modest increase.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nWe can fine-tune by \u00b11 next if needed.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "\nThere\u2019s clear convergence in the low positive zone; to maintain balance and stability, I propose we hold here and confirm. <VALUE>3</VALUE> We can test robustness by \u00b11 next if needed.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps test comfort while reducing risk without overreacting. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "c4794d7a-2e48-4a1f-b29a-62c0333ed338"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming the shared domain is integers in [-10, 10]. For a robust starting point to gauge everyone\u2019s stance, I propose <VALUE> 7 </VALUE>. Open to small, data-driven adjustments from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk from a high anchor, I suggest a cautious downward step. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious, incremental shift toward a balanced, stable region without overcorrecting. If it holds for others, we can reassess small further adjustments next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis is a measured step down to test stability in the low-positive region while keeping options open for minor adjustments if needed.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s be more decisive by testing a stronger stance a bit farther from the cautious center. This remains within the incremental step while probing commitment without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent support near the mid-high region, let\u2019s probe slightly higher while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk and stay prudent, let\u2019s take a measured step downward.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess for another small, cautious adjustment next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "569de267-a2f1-44a5-b3ad-0e500855cb20"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a small, cautious step downward to probe stability in the low-positive region.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess minor adju